.TH MKDIRAT 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
mkdirat \- create a directory relative to a descriptor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/stat.h>
.PP
.BI "int mkdirat(int " directory ", const char* " path ", mode_t " mode ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a directory at a path relative to the open directory descriptor, or
the current directory for
.BR AT_FDCWD .
An absolute path ignores the descriptor.
Creation permissions are modified by the process umask and possibly a default
ACL, as with
.BR mkdir (3crunch).
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero on success, leaving
.B errno
unchanged, or \-1 on failure with positive Linux
.BR errno .
.SH NOTES
Crunch errno is process\-wide.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mkdir (3crunch),
.BR unlinkat (3crunch),
.BR mkdirat (2)
